patients received a fixed dosage of 10 mg daily for ten days. Haloperidol was well tolerated by the patients; there were
no serious adverse reactions. The data indicated that the regimens had similar therapeutic efficacy, suggesting that    
acutely ill schizophrenic patients respond to a wide range of doses of haloperidol but that onset of response and       
efficacy are not increased in most patients by providing a high initial loading dosage. Adequate, safe dosage must be   
