of the treatment effect, reduce statistical power, and restrict the generalizability of results. The extent of the      
problem of attrition in central nervous system (CNS) trials is considered here and its consequences are examined. The   
taxonomy of missingness mechanisms is then briefly reviewed in order to introduce issues underlying the choice of data  
analytic strategies appropriate for RCTs with various forms of incomplete data. The convention of using last observation
carried forward to accommodate attrition is discouraged because its assumptions are typically inappropriate for CNS     
