evidence suggests these are not always addressed in an optimal manner. Aims and objectives This report describes a      
systematic review of methods for evaluating cluster-based interventions. There were three objectives: to review the     
methodological literature and synthesise the findings into a checklist of practical use; to evaluate existing practice  
